mail4agent-vodozemac
Copyright 2026 the mail4agent authors

This product includes a reduced, modified fork of "vodozemac", a Rust
implementation of the Olm and Megolm cryptographic ratchets and the SAS
(Short Authentication String) device-verification protocol used by Matrix.

Upstream project:   https://github.com/matrix-org/vodozemac
Upstream tag:        0.10.0
Upstream commit:     bb39ec65357989f975e0d47f9fb35e0656180151
Upstream license:    Apache License, Version 2.0

Copyright 2021-2024 The Matrix.org Foundation C.I.C.
Copyright 2021-2024 Damir Jelic, Denis Kasak, and the vodozemac contributors

This fork removes the `ecies`, `hazmat`, and `pk_encryption` modules, the
`libolm-compat` and MSC3814 device-dehydration code paths, and the `olm-rs`
(C libolm FFI) dev-dependency and every test that depends on it; it keeps
`olm`, `megolm`, `types`, `cipher`, `utilities`, and `sas`. Every modified source file carries a notice saying so. See FORK.md for
the itemized list of local changes and the upstream-delta-review procedure.

